 "name": "seers-chart",
 "about": "Eorzea on the game's own world map (ui/map/world/01, the Adventure map's painting): Aldenard and Vylbrand with Ishgard, Gridania, Ala Mhigo, Mor Dhona, Ul'dah and Limsa Lominsa, the chart's dragons, ships, kraken and compass roses, read as a seer's star chart. The map's parchment sea sinks to a deep amethyst night (a tone of 0.55 outside the land) and the land keeps its painted relief under an aether-teal region; the ley lines are drawn over it in pale aether from Mor Dhona's heart to each city and on out to sea, with the cities joined round the rim, and a small star of light where each city's lines meet. Crop [80, 888, 760, 570]: the texture's painted band is y 588-1458 of 2048, so the crop ends on the map's own lower border (the bucket's strip) and keeps Old Sharlayan's label off the board; Ul'dah, the lowest city, sits at y 446. A faint board-wide glow (radius 2000) keeps the dark land off sRGB 0-1 (3-1's fix for the converter's gate, MR 3 round 1, B1). The north-east cloud sea is cut out of the land mask by a poly, since its dark gaps read as land.",
